# fnp-sales-analysis
sales analysis using microsoft excel


FNP Sales (1,000 orders, 100 customers, ₹35.2 lakh in 2023)

Insights:

1) Four months bring in 68% of revenue: February (Valentine’s), March (Holi), August (Raksha Bandhan) and November (Diwali). January is the weakest at 2.7%.

2) Anniversary is the top occasion at ₹6.7 lakh (19%), then Raksha Bandhan (18%) and Holi (16%). Raksha Bandhan has the highest average order at ₹4,785, against ₹2,740 for Birthday. Raksha Bandhan and “All Occasions” orders are worth about 50% more than the rest.

3) Colors is the top category (29% of revenue), followed by Soft Toys (21%) and Sweets (21%). Product mix shifts by occasion. Holi is mostly Colors, Diwali is mostly Sweets, and Raksha Bandhan is mostly Soft Toys and Sweets.
 
4) Delivery is slow for gifting. The average is 5.5 days, and 41% of orders take 7–10 days. Peak occasions get no faster delivery (Diwali 4.9 days, Holi 5.8). For time-sensitive gifts, that is the biggest service gap.
 
5) Customer behaviour: Tuesday has the highest revenue and Sunday the most orders. Order volume peaks in the evening (7–9 PM) and early morning (7–9 AM), which suits timed promotions. Spending is split evenly between genders.
